# The two globs above are filename-substring matches with no extension/path
# scoping, so they also silently swallow legitimately-named test files (e.g.
# test_developer_platform_api_keys.py, which tests API-key creation and
# contains no real secret — Gitleaks + its own `gitleaks:allow` annotation
# are what actually guard against a real leaked key there, same as every
# other test fixture in this repo). Confirmed via `git status --ignored`
# that this was the only file caught. Scoped to *.py (not a bare **) so
# this doesn't also resurrect __pycache__/ dirs nested under backend/tests,
# which must stay ignored.
!backend/tests/**/*.py

